2026-10-30 07:48:31 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 20, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out this problem step by step. So, Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Then next week, he paints 1/4 the number he did this week. The question is asking how many ceilings will be left to paint after next week.\n\nFirst, let me make sure I understand the problem correctly. There are two parts: painting 28 ceilings total, with 12 painted this week, and then next week painting 1/4 the number he did this week. Then, subtract that number from the total number left to paint, which is initially 28, minus 12, then subtracting 1/4 of 12.\n\nLet me break it down:\n\nTotal ceilings initially: 28\n\nPainted this week: 12\n\nSo, the remaining ceilings after this week: 28 - 12 = 16\n\nNext week, he paints 1/4 of 12. Let me calculate that first. 1/4 of 12 is 3. Because 12 divided by 4 is 3.\n\nSo, he paints 3 ceilings next week. But wait, is 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week, meaning 12 divided by 4? Yes, so 12 divided by 4 is 3. So next week he paints 3. Then, the remaining ceilings after next week would be the ones already painted this week minus the ones painted next week. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, the remaining after this week is 16, which includes the ones he paints this week, and then he paints 3 next week. So the total remaining would be 16 - 3 = 13. Therefore, there will be 13 ceilings left to paint.\n\nLet me check again:\n\nTotal ceilings: 28\n\nPainted this week: 12. So remaining: 16\n\nPainted next week: 1/4 of 12 = 3. So remaining after next week: 16 - 3 = 13.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can think of total remaining after next week as 28 - 12 - (1/4 * 12). Which is 28 - 12 - 3. So 16 - 3 is 13. Yep, same answer.\n\nBut maybe I should check if the problem says \"he paints 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week.\" So if he did 12 this week, then next week he paints 3. That seems correct. So subtracting 3 from the remaining 16 gives 13.\n\nIs there any chance I made a mistake here? Let me recast the problem in another way. Let me calculate how much he paints next week: 1/4 of 12 is 3. So total ceilings painted over both weeks is 12 + 3 = 15. The remaining would be 28 - 15 = 13. Same result. So that's another way to look at it. So yes, answer is 13.\n\nI think that's solid. So the answer is 13 ceilings will be left to paint.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{13}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many ceilings will be left to paint after next week, let's follow the problem step by step:\n\n1. **Total ceilings to paint:** 28\n\n2. **Ceilings painted this week:** 12\n\n3. **Ceilings remaining after this week:**  \n   $ 28 - 12 = 16 $\n\n4. **How many ceilings he will paint next week:**  \n   He paints $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the ceilings he painted this week, which is:  \n   $ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 = 3 $\n\n5. **Ceilings remaining after next week:**  \n   $ 16 - 3 = 13 $\n\n---\n\nThus, after next week, Michelangelo will paint **13** ceilings left to paint.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{13}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 9295, 2003, 11, 566, 686, 6177, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 1521], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 5005, 1790, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 566, 1521, 419, 2003, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161, 1246, 1657, 55714, 686]}
