ame as 7*(28) inches squared. Which again gives 196. \n\nI don't see any errors in my reasoning. Both methods lead to the same answer. So I think the area of the rectangle is 196 square inches. The final answer should be in a box, so \\boxed{196}. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe area of the rectangle is \\boxed{196}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the area of the rectangle, we begin by using the given information: the rectangle is 7 inches wide and is 4 times as long as it is wide.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the Length of the Rectangle\n\nSince the rectangle's side that is 4 times the width is the length, and the width is 7 inches:\n\n$$\n\\text{Length} = 4 \\times 7 = 28 \\text{ inches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the Area Formula for a Rectangle\n\nThe area of a rectangle is calculated as:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{width} \\times \\text{length}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = 7 \\times 28 = 196\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\nThe area of the rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{196}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "You draw a rectangle that is 7 inches wide. It is 4 times as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle?", "answer": "The length of the rectangle is 4 * 7 inches = <<4*7=28>>28 inches.\nThe area of the rectangle is 7 inches * 28 inches = <<7*28=196>>196 square inches.\n#### 196", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: You draw a rectangle that is 7 inches wide. It is 4 times as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["196"], "solution": "196"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 1446, 4038, 264, 22756, 429, 374, 220, 22, 14924, 6884, 13, 1084, 374, 220, 19, 3039, 438, 1293, 438, 432, 374, 6884, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 3082, 315, 279, 22756, 5267, 36842, 25, 15164