em says the average number of answers is three times the number of questions. So if each user posts 3 questions per hour, then the total number of questions per hour is 200 * 3. Therefore, the average number of answers per user is (3 times total number of questions per hour) divided by total number of users? Wait, no. Wait, more carefully:\n\nLet me think again. Let me denote:\n\nLet Q be the number of questions each member asks. So each member asks Q questions. Also, the average number of answers is three times Q. So total answers would be 200 users * average answers per user. But average answers per user is 3Q. Therefore total answers would be 200 * 3Q. Therefore, total answers = 600Q.\n\nSimilarly, total questions per hour would be 200 * 3Q, as before. So if we can find Q, multiply by 600 to get questions and answers total?\n\nWait, but the problem says \"the average number of answers posted by each member is three times as many as the number of questions asked.\" So maybe the total number of answers is 3 times total questions? But each user has a certain number of questions and answers.\n\nWait, perhaps the question is phrased as: \"If each user posts an average of 3 questions per hour, calculate the total number of questions and answers posted on the forum by its users in a day.\"\n\nSo total number of questions and answers on the forum in a day. So first, find total number of questions asked by all users in a day, and total number of answers asked by all users in a day. Then add them together?\n\nSo let's start with that.\n\nFirst, total number of questions asked by all users in a day. Each user posts 3 questions per hour. In one day, there are 24 hours. Therefore, total questions per day would be 24 * 200 * 3.\n\nSimilarly, total answers posted by all users in a day would be 24 * 200 * (average answers per user per day). But average answers per user per day? Since average answers per user is 3 times the number of questions each member posted per hour.\n\nWait