he answer is 26.\n\nAlternatively, if someone thought that the 8 hours is the total time she can use, meaning that she builds all fences during that time, so 8 hours is 480 minutes, number of fences is 16, total is 26.\n\nYes, I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{26}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many fences Abigail would have built in total, we begin by analyzing the given information step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate time spent on the initial 10 fences\n\n- Each fence took **30 minutes**.\n- Abigail built **10 fences**.\n- Time taken for these 10 fences:", "source_record": {"question": "Abigail built 10 fences. Each fence took her 30 minutes to build. If she builds fences for the next 8 hours, how many fences would she have built in total?", "answer": "8*60 = <<8*60=480>>480 minutes are in the next 8 hours.\nAbigail builds 480/30 = <<480/30=16>>16 fences.\nAbigail will have built 10+16 = <<10+16=26>>26 fences in total.\n#### 26", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Abigail built 10 fences. Each fence took her 30 minutes to build. If she builds fences for the next 8 hours, how many fences would she have built in total?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["26"], "solution": "26"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 3680, 84206, 5798, 220, 16, 15, 69155, 13, 8886, 24650, 3867, 1059, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 311, 1936, 13, 1416, 1340, 22111, 69155, 369, 279, 1790, 220, 23, 4115, 11, 1246, 1657, 69155, 1035, 1340, 614, 5798], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 576, 3491, 2727, 429, 3680, 84206, 5798, 220, 16, 15, 69155, 13, 8886, 315, 1846, 3867, 1059, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 311, 1936, 13, 4695, 11, 1340, 1083, 22111, 69155, 369, 279, 1790, 220, 23, 4115, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 69155, 1340, 